1.  start epics screens
2.  start temp logger
3.  start repeatability test
4.  low level motor control
5.  changing home switch
6.  modifying gnirsConfig




1.  start epics screens

	from an ace or otter window
	
	nirsSeqStart


2.  start temp logger
	This program will not overwrite an existing file, so you must select a
	 unique filename

	from components controller screen

	startLog 15, "/home/gemini/gnirs/data/test/temps.log"

	the first parameter is the time between reads
	the second parameter is a unique filename with full path

	'killLog'			 to stop logging

	you must stop the logging before the computer is rebooted or turned off 
	or the data will be lost

3. repeatability test

	This must be started from an otter screen
	

	otter <  cd /home/gemini/gnirs/control/data/test

	otter <   python -i gnirs.py

	>>> homeTest (7,250000,-250000,3,50)


	parameter 1: motor number
	parameter 2: step position
	parameter 3: step position #2
	parameter 4: times to repeat test
	parameter 5:  # of steps for bracketing home position


	control-C stops a running script (it is safest to reboot the system 
		after a control-c)
	control-D exits out of the python shell and returns control to the 
		components controller screen

	
4. low level motor control
	from cc window

	-> motorOn 7
	-> cmd 7
	>

	some useful  commands
	LF - turn limits off
	VL# - set velocity (eg. VL1000)
	AC# - set acceleration
	MA# GO - move to absolute position
	MR# GO - move relative position
	SD - stop motion


5.  changing home switch
	useAlt 7,1

	parameter 1: motor number
	parameter 2: 0 = primary, 1= secondary


6.  modifying Config parameters
	change gnirsConfig file
	run 'gmake' from an irlab account on ace otter or kiwi
	open initCad epics screen
	press mark button
 
	make sure system is in idle state
	press start button

	wait for system to go back to idle

	
